<title>YEMEN: Over 100 graduates protest at Yemen gov't office.</title>
<headline>Over 100 graduates protest at Yemen gov't office.</headline>
<dateline>SANAA 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Over 100 Yemeni graduates from oil and mineral faculties demonstrated in front of a key government building in Sanaa on Wednesday, demanding jobs after the oil ministry refused to employ them.</p>
<p>The graduates demonstrated in front of the cabinet's offices during the ministers' weekly session, saying they were being denied jobs despite written orders by Yemen's President Ali Abdullah Saleh.</p>
<p>&quot;There were over 150 of us, and we have been unemployed since we graduated last year from universities all over the world,&quot; 28-year-old Abdul Mohsen Hassan Ali told Reuters.</p>
<p>Yemen, a small oil producer, suffers from unemployment ranging from 30 to 50 percent.</p>
